          "label": "Sharm vs Cairo",
          "type": "script",
          "text": "In Sharm, everyone speaks English, things run more or less on tourist time, and the streets are quiet by midnight. Cairo never sleeps. And people are different — more direct, louder, funnier. Cairo has this incredible sense of humor, dark and self-aware. Cairenes joke about the traffic, about the price of bread, about politics. It's a very alive city. Don't be surprised if a shopkeeper makes you laugh before you even ask the price of anything."
